            "level": {
                "value": 4
            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Stories abound of fey who steal away people, and many have a grain of truth. No fey embodies the fear in such tales quite like the bagman. These pale, greasy fey are gluttons who delight in eating sentient creatures. They capture their prey within bloody sacks, spiriting them away to murder the victim and devour everything but their fat. That, they save, rendering it into foul alchemical elixirs which they then gleefully sell to the unsuspecting settlement from which they kidnapped their victim.</p>\n<p>Bagmen don't need to eat for sustenance, nor do they care for wealth—they merely enjoy spreading suffering. They're masters of disguise and often appear as traveling peddlers of medicinals, wearing deep cloaks and wide-brimmed hats, cruelly offering products to townsfolk crafted from missing loved ones.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
